USE health_ai_platform;

-- ============================================================
-- Real policy content for the 5 core Management knowledge_docs
-- (v1/v2/v3 of each = 15 rows total), replacing the Faker
-- gibberish generated by generate_seed_data.py.
-- ============================================================

-- --- KPI Definitions Reference -----------------------------
UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Every department-level report uses three standardized KPIs so results are comparable across departments: volume (the count of primary transactions processed in the period, e.g. claims adjudicated, tickets closed), avg_turnaround_days (mean time from intake to resolution for the period), and sla_pct (the percentage of transactions that met the department''s published SLA target for that transaction type). A department may track additional metrics internally, but only these three standardized fields are reported in the kpi_summary field of a management_reports record, so cross-department comparison stays meaningful. sla_pct is always calculated against the SLA target in effect during the reporting period, not the current SLA target, if the target changed mid-period.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'KPI Definitions Reference';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 2 adds a data-quality floor to the standardized KPIs in v1: a report with fewer than 20 underlying transactions in the period is flagged as low-confidence rather than reported with the same weight as a high-volume department, since a small sample can produce a misleadingly extreme sla_pct or avg_turnaround_days. This revision also clarifies that avg_turnaround_days uses business days, not calendar days, consistent with how individual departments already measure their own internal SLA targets.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'KPI Definitions Reference v2';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 3 adds a trend indicator alongside the point-in-time figures in v1 and v2: each KPI is now reported with a direction (improving, stable, declining) relative to the trailing three-period average, not just the current-period value in isolation, since a single-period snapshot was found to obscure whether a department was actually trending in a concerning direction. This revision also formalizes the low-confidence flag from v2 as a required field on the report itself, not just an informal caveat in prepared_by notes.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'KPI Definitions Reference v3';

-- --- Quarterly Business Review Template -----------------------------
UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'The quarterly business review for each department covers four sections in order: (1) KPI summary against target for the quarter, using the standardized fields from the KPI Definitions Reference, (2) notable variances with root cause where known, (3) initiatives in progress and their status, and (4) risks and asks for leadership support. Reviews are prepared by the department director and presented to executive leadership within 15 business days of quarter close. A department reporting a declining KPI trend for two consecutive quarters must include a specific remediation plan in section 3, not just note the decline.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Quarterly Business Review Template';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 2 shortens the preparation window in v1 from 15 to 10 business days after quarter close, since most of the underlying department data (per the standardized KPI fields) is already available well before that deadline in practice. This revision also adds a required cross-department dependency section: if a department risk depends on another department resolving something first (e.g. Claims turnaround affecting Finance loss ratio reporting), that dependency must be named explicitly rather than described only in general terms.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Quarterly Business Review Template v2';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 3 adds a standing follow-up mechanism to the remediation-plan requirement in v1: any remediation plan committed to in one quarterly review must be explicitly revisited (completed, in progress, or abandoned with reason) in the following quarter review, rather than the plan simply disappearing from the document once written. This revision also adds an executive-summary requirement at the top of the template, capped at 150 words, since leadership feedback indicated the four-section detail in v1 was useful but needed a short synthesis up front.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Quarterly Business Review Template v3';

-- --- Departmental Reporting Calendar -----------------------------
UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Monthly departmental KPI reports are due by the 10th business day of the following month. Quarterly business reviews follow the separate, longer timeline in the Quarterly Business Review Template. Ad hoc reports (a specific request from leadership outside the standard cycle) do not follow this calendar and are due on whatever timeline the requester specifies, but must still use the standardized kpi_summary fields where applicable so they remain comparable to the regular reporting cadence. A department that will miss the monthly deadline must notify the Management reporting team at least 2 business days in advance with a revised date, rather than simply submitting late without notice.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Departmental Reporting Calendar';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 2 adds a grace period to the monthly deadline in v1: a report submitted within 2 business days after the 10th-business-day deadline is accepted without the advance-notice requirement, since a short, unannounced delay was found to be common and did not warrant the same escalation as a longer miss. This revision also adds a mid-month data snapshot requirement for departments whose monthly KPI has shown two consecutive declining periods (per the KPI Definitions Reference trend indicator), so leadership is not surprised by a third consecutive decline only at month end.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Departmental Reporting Calendar v2';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 3 adds a holiday-adjusted deadline calculation: the "10th business day" standard from v1 and v2 is calculated using the actual published holiday calendar for the reporting year, not a generic business-day count, since December and other holiday-heavy months were consistently producing missed deadlines under the simple count. This revision also formalizes the ad hoc report exception from v1 with a required intake log, so every ad hoc request and its actual delivery date is tracked centrally rather than existing only as an email thread between the requester and the department.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Departmental Reporting Calendar v3';

-- --- Executive Escalation Policy -----------------------------
UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'A department director should escalate to executive leadership when a KPI falls more than 10 percentage points below target for a single period, when a cross-department dependency risk (per the Quarterly Business Review Template) is not being resolved on a reasonable timeline, or when a situation has member-facing or regulatory risk regardless of KPI impact. Escalations should go through the standing weekly leadership meeting for non-urgent matters, or directly to the relevant executive sponsor for anything time-sensitive. An escalation is not a substitute for the standard reporting cadence — it supplements it for the specific issue, not a replacement for the regular KPI report.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Executive Escalation Policy';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 2 adds a specific threshold to the general "member-facing or regulatory risk" trigger in v1: any issue with a plausible path to a regulatory reporting obligation (a compliance deadline, a required notice to members) is escalated within 24 hours of identification regardless of severity, since the original general language was being interpreted inconsistently across departments. This revision also adds a written follow-up requirement: every direct-to-executive escalation must be documented in a brief written summary within 48 hours, even though the initial escalation itself may have been a phone call or an in-person conversation.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Executive Escalation Policy v2';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 3 adds an escalation-fatigue safeguard: if the same department escalates the same underlying issue more than twice within a quarter without resolution, the issue is automatically elevated to a standing agenda item at the executive leadership meeting rather than continuing as a series of individual escalations, since repeated unresolved escalations were found to lose leadership attention over time rather than gaining urgency. This revision also clarifies the KPI threshold in v1: the 10-percentage-point trigger applies to sla_pct specifically, and a separate, lower 5-percentage-point threshold applies when the department has already shown a declining trend per the KPI Definitions Reference.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Executive Escalation Policy v3';

-- --- Budget Variance Review SOP -----------------------------
UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Departmental budget variance is reviewed monthly alongside the standard KPI reporting cycle. A variance greater than 5 percent of the monthly budgeted amount, in either direction, requires a written explanation from the department director; variances over 15 percent require executive sign-off before the following month closes. Favorable variances (spending less than budgeted) still require explanation above the threshold, not just unfavorable ones, since an unexplained favorable variance can indicate a deferred expense or a data error as easily as genuine efficiency. Variance review references the same GL account structure used in Finance''s reporting, so the two teams'' figures reconcile without separate mapping.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Budget Variance Review SOP';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 2 lowers the executive sign-off threshold in v1 from 15 percent to 10 percent for expense categories tied to vendor contracts specifically, since vendor-related variances were found more likely to reflect a genuine contractual issue worth executive visibility than other expense categories. This revision also adds a rolling three-month view to the standard monthly review: a department with three consecutive small unfavorable variances (each under the 5 percent threshold individually) is flagged for review even though no single month triggered the standard threshold, since the cumulative effect was found to be a meaningful early signal.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Budget Variance Review SOP v2';

UPDATE knowledge_docs SET content = 'Revision 3 adds a forecast-accuracy component alongside the variance thresholds in v1 and v2: a department whose actual spending deviates significantly from its own most recent forecast (not just from the original annual budget) is also flagged, since a department can stay within its original annual budget threshold while still demonstrating poor month-to-month forecasting discipline. This revision also formalizes the rolling three-month flag from v2 into the same written-explanation requirement as a single-month threshold breach, rather than treating it as a softer, informal review.'
WHERE dept_id = 9 AND title = 'Budget Variance Review SOP v3';
